{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tan-goldenrod-drever","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe scripts cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py:1–28, 41–46, 110–125, 132–136, 155–163, 180–185, 281–285` — Preserve two questions/output, project-before-fields ordering, bounded poll, shared readiness, evidence on failure. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py:1–73, 91–118, 128–138, 167–177, 194–207, 235–254, 287–326` — Preserve post-project precondition, concise measurement citation, inventory discriminator, bounded/fail-closed semantics, success/failure evidence. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/main_health_report.py:2–25` — Preserve scheduled-main purpose, green/red fields, fail-soft last-green lookup. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/mutation_gate.py:26–30, 587–595, 664–668` — Preserve invocation-independent import, every shard-code execution sandboxed, basetemp existence, venv read-only. Consumer: affected prose is source-only.\n- `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:2–32, 68–101, 250–255` — Preserve OS mechanisms, functional enforcement probes, explicit waiver/fail-closed policy, two-signal Seatbelt proof, external caution citation. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/probe_rebar.py:555–570` — Preserve exact expected symmetric difference and conditional signature-field intersection. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py:2–22` — Preserve read-only inputs/linkage, defaults, malformed-record behavior, reproducibility pointer. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/release_guards.py:2–23, 75–82` — Preserve version/manifest, ancestry, environment protection, and publisher-description contracts. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/retarget_jira_project.py:2–30` — Preserve stale bindings/snapshot behavior, dry-run/apply, backups/tag stripping, post-preview safety. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py:2–30` — Preserve inputs/output, timeout-annotation distinction, comment-only/no-vote behavior. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"40d7-eca8-8726-4b14","parent_id":"3de8-31a0-25ef-456d","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in scripts — cohort 04: jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe–summarize_ci_failures"}